questions.workedExample:
1. SQLite: a failed statement is undone, but the transaction continues, so the audit insert and COMMIT work.
2. PostgreSQL: any error puts the transaction into an aborted state. Every following statement fails until ROLLBACK, and COMMIT acts as ROLLBACK.
3. Fix with a savepoint:

```sql
BEGIN;
SAVEPOINT try_user;
INSERT INTO users ...;
-- on error:
ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT try_user;
INSERT INTO audit_log ...;
COMMIT;
```

4. Or avoid the error: `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (email) DO NOTHING RETURNING id` and check whether a row came back.

